1sai|v|To weigh or measure according to a scale; to measure; also, to grade or vary according to a scale or system. ; To strip or clear of scale or scales; as, to scale a fish; to scale the inside of a boiler. ; To take off in thin layers or scales, as tartar from the teeth; to pare off, as a surface. ; To scatter; to spread. ; To clean, as the inside of a cannon, by the explosion of a small quantity of powder. ; To separate and come off in thin layers or laminae; as, some sandstone scales by exposure. ; To separate; to scatter. ; To climb by a ladder, or as if by a ladder; to ascend by steps or by climbing; to clamber up; as, to scale the wall of a fort. ; To lead up by steps; to ascend.	o:269d,26,4~269d,26,4	d:mpf,18,3;t9l,10,3~t9l,10,3;mpf,18,3	D:1m57,37,2;yff,31,4;45q,23,4;169d,18,1;mpf,12,2;1cfa,9,3;1kbj,9,3;10y7,8,1;467,8,2;k0e,7,5~k0e,7,5;45q,23,4;yff,31,4;1kbj,9,3;1cfa,9,3;467,8,2;1m57,37,2;mpf,12,2;10y7,8,1;169d,18,1
