1siy|n|A shoal; a multitude; as, a school of fish. ; A place for learned intercourse and instruction; an institution for learning; an educational establishment; a place for acquiring knowledge and mental training; as, the school of the prophets. ; A place of primary instruction; an establishment for the instruction of children; as, a primary school; a common school; a grammar school. ; A session of an institution of instruction. ; One of the seminaries for teaching logic, metaphysics, and theology, which were formed in the Middle Ages, and which were characterized by academical disputations and subtilties of reasoning. ; The room or hall in English universities where the examinations for degrees and honors are held. ; An assemblage of scholars; those who attend upon instruction in a school of any kind; a body of pupils. ; The disciples or followers of a teacher; those who hold a common doctrine, or accept the same teachings; a sect or denomination in philosophy, theology, science, medicine, politics, etc. ; The canons, precepts, or body of opinion or practice, sanctioned by the authority of a particular class or age; as, he was a gentleman of the old school. ; Figuratively, any means of knowledge or discipline; as, the school of experience.	a:vj6,92,3;1d7i,66,4;2777,58,5;1l93,56,3;5ke,50,5;b88,48,4;1d7l,47,3;7of,46,2;geq,46,3;l9,42,5;1phv,42,5;1qrn,42,3;nfm,41,40;vjo,38,219;1px2,36,5~xvm,32,709;vjo,38,219;nfm,41,40;1t2w,22,38;18me,25,37;19iy,24,35;1lk9,5,26;253x,14,20;1l94,28,20;1o1i,29,10;22ae,25,8;vja,0,7;lp7,14,7;1p1y,27,7;1lef,18,7	v:19j3,61,3;1d7l,47,3;27f3,37,4;5d6,31,5;5d9,30,8;8c2,30,3;vjr,21,3;fjm,20,2;l9,19,1;vjo,17,50;28a0,15,5;5d2,15,4;isy,15,2;27iz,14,4;ru5,10,4~vjo,17,50;5d9,30,8;mbh,9,6;28a0,15,5;5d6,31,5;ru5,10,4;27f3,37,4;5d2,15,4;27iz,14,4;1d7l,47,3;vjr,21,3;8c2,30,3;19j3,61,3;psr,9,2;isy,15,2	V:g3t,41,5;1m4,39,6;9lp,39,3;t33,36,3;2024,31,4;xza,22,5;1o1k,19,5;1o1i,19,5;13gi,18,5;460,15,5;28a0,15,5;20wp,14,5;1fjv,14,5;xze,13,1;1qbo,13,1~20za,1,13;1p